<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="notes-week-01">
  <title>Example</title>

  <p>
    Welcome to <pretext/>! According to Pythagoras, <m>a^2 + b^2 = c^2</m>.
    But he also thought <m>\sqrt{2}</m> was rational, so maybe we shouldn't listen to him.
  </p>

  <p>
    Let's collect some info about squares:
  </p>

  <table>
    <title>Perfect Squares</title>

    <tabular halign="center">
      <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
        <cell><m>n</m></cell>
        <cell><m>n^2</m></cell>
      </row>

      <row>
        <cell>1</cell>
        <cell>1</cell>
      </row>

      <row>
        <cell>2</cell>
        <cell>4</cell>
      </row>

      <row>
        <cell>3</cell>
        <cell>9</cell>
      </row>

      <row>
        <cell><m>\vdots</m></cell>
        <cell><m>\vdots</m></cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>
  </table>

  <theorem xml:id="thm-Pythagorean">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Suppose a right triangle has side lengths <m>a, b</m> and hypotenuse length <m>c</m>.
        Then:
        <md>
          <mrow> a^2 + b^2 = c^2. </mrow>
        </md>
      </p>
    </statement>
  </theorem>
</section>